{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair","id":244059,"title":"Sidereal Job Fair!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-29T09:37:52-07:00","id":244059,"title":"Sidereal Job Fair!","content":"As presented in previous editions, Sidereals basically have two options: Work for the Bureau of Destiny for life, or go Ronin. For the new edition, I'd like to see more variety in their choices. <br /> <br /> Starting with the Celestial Bureaucracy, must all Sids only work for the B. of Destiny? Why not open up their options so that they can go to work in the other Bureaus? Chosen of Battles should have the chance to work under E-Naluna's Dept of Warfare, or with the Aerial Legion, and I'd think that Chosen of Journeys would be a natural fit for the B. of Nature. Those are just the obvious ones, there are plenty of gods whose domains would benefit from one of the Maiden's Chosen working with them, either to further their aims in Creation, or just working in any of the innumerable businesses the gods operate in Yu-Shan. For that matter, one can easily imagine Viziers being very valued as enforcers or accountants for the god mobs running the derelict slums of heaven. I just think that it's a shame to detail Heaven's society so much, then to say &quot;but your PCs can only work in this one area&quot;. <br /> <br /> Sidereals should also be able to find work in the Underworld or Malfeas, much like Gemstone Ocean Hero. Just walk in and set up shop as a Stranger, providing some valuable service to ghosts/demons, without actually serving the agenda of the Neverborn/Yozis as an Akuma or whatever. <br /> <br /> Lastly, Seers should be able to have more of an impact on Creation. Arcane Fate makes running things there difficult, but it should never be seen as an absolute bar to exercising influence among mankind. Since Sidereals are generally not people who feel comfortable in the spotlight anyway, it really aids their &quot;power behind the throne&quot; methodology. Let's see more Siddies behind mortal families, organizations, social movements, not for Heaven's Plan, but for their own reasons (not to make mindless pawns of the mortals; the leaders probably know all about the &quot;mysterious benefactor&quot; they are partners with).<br /> <br /> That's about all I can come up with. Any other ideas for things for Sidereals to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T09:59:14-07:00","id":244101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair#post244059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting with the Celestial Bureaucracy, must all Sids only work for the B. of Destiny? Why not open up their options so that they can go to work in the other Bureaus? Chosen of Battles should have the chance to work under E-Naluna's Dept of Warfare, or with the Aerial Legion, and I'd think that Chosen of Journeys would be a natural fit for the B. of Nature. Those are just the obvious ones, there are plenty of gods whose domains would benefit from one of the Maiden's Chosen working with them, either to further their aims in Creation, or just working in any of the innumerable businesses the gods operate in Yu-Shan. For that matter, one can easily imagine Viziers being very valued as enforcers or accountants for the god mobs running the derelict slums of heaven. I just think that it's a shame to detail Heaven's society so much, then to say &quot;but your PCs can only work in this one area&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of an internship or work experience deal where a newly exalted Chosen of Serenity, say, can go apprentice under Burning Feather for a while -- the Sidereal gets experience and tutelage, the god gets a plum in the Sidereal pudding. <br /> I think there's also a lot more room for Sidereal diplomats, talking to Hell/the Underworld on behalf of Heaven. Someone who visits Verumipra every once in a while, someone besides the Green Lady who takes time to actually talk to the Dual Monarchs (not to mention visiting the Calendar of Setesh, like a rubbernecker at a car crash).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:00:22-07:00","id":244105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair#post244059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting with the Celestial Bureaucracy, must all Sids only work for the B. of Destiny?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally - after all, it's where the folks who dick around with the Loom of Fate <i>work</i>. <b>Must</b> all McDonald's employees work at McDonald's restaurants? Well, no - in fact, a fair number of them don't - but generally, it's why you're not going to find them working at Burger King.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:07:04-07:00","id":244114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair?p=244105#post244105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally - after all, it's where the folks who dick around with the Loom of Fate <i>work</i>. <b>Must</b> all McDonald's employees work at McDonald's restaurants? Well, no - in fact, a fair number of them don't - but generally, it's why you're not going to find them working at Burger King.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might raise the question, then, should the other Bureaus have access to the Loom of Fate for their own business? I know they don't now, but putting aside what we know to speculate about how the setting might be changed, would it ruin anything if they DID? It would give them a reason to actively seek to lure Sidereals away and into their service, which plays up the heavenly politics angle Sid stories are supposed to embrace. And, as I think you allude to, it may even be possible for Sids to work two jobs in two different Bureaus, if they think they can handle the time and workload.<br /> <br /> I still see this as a minority, btw. Most Sids will still work for the Bureau and Division they are native to. I'd just like there to be more options available to open up the setting for PCs to explore some more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:36:51-07:00","id":244147,"title":"","content":"There are definitely stories to tell about Sidereals working elsewhere. That said, I find myself raising an eyebrow at the implication that working for the Bureau of Destiny means one is cordoned off from a lot. To do their job and see Destiny carried out, Sidereal stories can have them working with and against potentially anyone in the Celestial Bureaucracy and their fields of interest, which in turn span the whole of Creation and realms beyond. Sidereals can find themselves working closely with gods outside the Bureau of Destiny -- or outside Yu-Shan altogether -- both on projects that concern the Bureau of Destiny and on personally decided initiatives. Not to say there isn't additional space opened or potential value in considering other contexts. But yeah, I feel it's important to recognize that this is an expansion added to an area that's already incredibly robust.<br /> <br /> Though I'll definitely agree there could be a few more examples of Sidereals highlighting some of these possibilities over the millennia. Expressing more of the vast diversity they can have would be very welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T10:57:43-07:00","id":244182,"title":"","content":"Being Ronin just means that you've specifically opted to leave the service of Heaven. Sidereals who opt to find some kind of service in the Underworld, or Malfeas or manipulating mortals in some manner other than according to the designs of Fate... those are all Ronin. Ronin basically defines what you aren't, not what you are.<br /> <br /> Of course, Sidereals in the service of Destiny should also be pursuing various projects in Creation and other places in order to fulfil those designs. As agents of Yu-Shan go, they're fairly hands-on. Heck, Chejop Kejak alone juggles being head of the Central Convention, membership on all of the special ones, being a special advisor to Nara-O, and managing all of his Bronze Faction concerns with being the secretary to most of the Mouths of Peace, a regular instructor at the Heptagram, and a direct collaborator with the Scarlet Empress and tutor to some of her children.<br /> <br /> Similarly, the idea that Sidereals never diffuse through the other Bureaus, or that they lack in influence upon the planning of Destiny, seems to underestimate how much of a bureaucracy the Celestial Order is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:36:39-07:00","id":244222,"title":"","content":"There's really nothing saying that a Sidereal can't be, say, Special Envoy to the Bureau of Seasons. They would still be employed by the Bureau of Destiny, but their day to day concerns would be less sitting around the Loom watching the Pattern Spiders and more making sure some shithead of a Twilight didn't divert all the rain in the East to water his weed patch.<br /> <br /> As for more personal influence in Creation...well, generally, as long as the Sidereal isn't disrupting planned destinies or abusing her Salary (and no one has been bribed to take an interest in her activities), what she does in her off hours are up to her.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T11:46:42-07:00","id":244234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair?p=244222#post244222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's really nothing saying that a Sidereal can't be, say, Special Envoy to the Bureau of Seasons. They would still be employed by the Bureau of Destiny, but their day to day concerns would be less sitting around the Loom watching the Pattern Spiders and more making sure some shithead of a Twilight didn't divert all the rain in the East to water his weed patch.</div> </div> </div> </div>...unless it's <i>really</i> good weed. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T12:05:10-07:00","id":244251,"title":"","content":"I really see it as 'Sidereals have two option: Working for the Bureau of Destiny, or doing something else (and being called a Ronin). A Chosen of Mars who becomes special attache to the Lord of Collating Records of North Battles, or a Chosen of Venus who spends her years assisting the varying gods of mating dances develop and update mating dances both have legitimate jobs in heaven, but they are considered ronin by other Sidereals. Also major slackers for blowing off their 'REAL' jobs working at the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> I figure most Sidereals intern in other departments, but most gods wouldn't accept a Sidereal out of distrust. Those that do have probably had to work really hard to leave, and are probably blocked from promotion by everyone, meaning many ronin head down to Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T12:06:37-07:00","id":244254,"title":"","content":"As I recall, taking hiatuses in which they build utilise their powers and connections in order to cultivate personal projects is considered one of the natural privileges of the Sidereal Exalted. Taking a personal interest in the dramas of your mortal descendants or the politics of the nation where you grew up, or cultivating a certain philosophy like it was a bonsai, or resolving a dispute you had with some Terrestrial god or fae lord or sea monster, these are the standard vacation package of somebody who lives for thousands of years and can sorcerously direct the course of lives and history. Just don't do anything that messes up the divine plan.<br /> <br /> Actually, can Sidereals build up sufficient good will to take time off equal to a mortal lifetime? You know, spend sixty or seventy years raising a family and holding down a job and being a pillar of the local community, that kind of thing? Certainly seems like something many people who can live for literal ages would go in for. They can even use resplendent destinies to be remembered as themselves (as I understand, that's the default for them anyway, a further form of identity needs to be actively cultivated; most Sidereals don't, because it doesn't suit their reason for assuming destinies in the first place, and there can be dangers if you're recognised within different destinies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T12:42:55-07:00","id":244274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair?p=244254#post244254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, taking hiatuses in which they build utilise their powers and connections in order to cultivate personal projects is considered one of the natural privileges of the Sidereal Exalted. Taking a personal interest in the dramas of your mortal descendants or the politics of the nation where you grew up, or cultivating a certain philosophy like it was a bonsai, or resolving a dispute you had with some Terrestrial god or fae lord or sea monster, these are the standard vacation package of somebody who lives for thousands of years and can sorcerously direct the course of lives and history. Just don't do anything that messes up the divine plan.<br /> <br /> Actually, can Sidereals build up sufficient good will to take time off equal to a mortal lifetime? You know, spend sixty or seventy years raising a family and holding down a job and being a pillar of the local community, that kind of thing? Certainly seems like something many people who can live for literal ages would go in for. They can even use resplendent destinies to be remembered as themselves (as I understand, that's the default for them anyway, a further form of identity needs to be actively cultivated; most Sidereals don't, because it doesn't suit their reason for assuming destinies in the first place, and there can be dangers if you're recognised within different destinies).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the book mentions that the department gets pissy if it's missing a crucial tactical asset for too long- but sometimes you've got to live life for yourself, y'know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T08:37:32-07:00","id":245346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/244059-sidereal-job-fair?p=244254#post244254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, taking hiatuses in which they build utilise their powers and connections in order to cultivate personal projects is considered one of the natural privileges of the Sidereal Exalted. Taking a personal interest in the dramas of your mortal descendants or the politics of the nation where you grew up, or cultivating a certain philosophy like it was a bonsai, or resolving a dispute you had with some Terrestrial god or fae lord or sea monster, these are the standard vacation package of somebody who lives for thousands of years and can sorcerously direct the course of lives and history. Just don't do anything that messes up the divine plan.<br /> <br /> Actually, can Sidereals build up sufficient good will to take time off equal to a mortal lifetime? You know, spend sixty or seventy years raising a family and holding down a job and being a pillar of the local community, that kind of thing? Certainly seems like something many people who can live for literal ages would go in for. They can even use resplendent destinies to be remembered as themselves (as I understand, that's the default for them anyway, a further form of identity needs to be actively cultivated; most Sidereals don't, because it doesn't suit their reason for assuming destinies in the first place, and there can be dangers if you're recognised within different destinies).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes and no. Sabbaticals range from about a week to five years, and it is explicitly said that NO Sidereal can work around that time limit. HOWEVER, there is also &quot;Detached Duty&quot;, where you can take an extended leave to attend to something Very Important (it is implied that this is what the Green Lady is doing). It's left up to the ST and player to decide what you need to do to get this (probably LOTS of Favors and the ability to spin what you want as The Needs of Creation), but there's no time limit on how long this can last. But your bosses/Oversight are probably watching you *very* carefully, so good luck trying to actually relax!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}